  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Repository/501372599/v1.20.0</id>
    <updated>2026-09-28T20:43:03Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://github.com/openfga/openfga/releases/tag/v1.20.0"/>
    <title>v1.20.0</title>
    <content type="html">&lt;h2&gt;What&#39;s Changed&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Added&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Added &lt;code&gt;WithServiceName&lt;/code&gt; server option to allow embedders to override the &lt;code&gt;serviceName&lt;/code&gt; field used for the &lt;code&gt;grpc_service&lt;/code&gt; label on OpenFGA&#39;s package-level Prometheus metrics and &lt;code&gt;telemetry.RPCInfo.Service&lt;/code&gt;. This enables multiple &lt;code&gt;Server&lt;/code&gt; instances in the same process to emit separate metric series. Note it does not rename the standard gRPC server metrics (e.g. &lt;code&gt;grpc_server_handled_total&lt;/code&gt;), whose labels are derived from the registered gRPC service. Use stable, low-cardinality names, as the value becomes a metric label. Defaults to &lt;code&gt;openfgav1.OpenFGAService_ServiceDesc.ServiceName&lt;/code&gt; when omitted (backward compatible). &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/openfga/openfga/pull/3265&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/openfga/openfga/pull/3265/hovercard&quot;&gt;#3265&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Fixed&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fixed a deadlock in ListUsers that caused a timeout with partial results when the number of union/intersection operands exceeded &lt;code&gt;OPENFGA_RESOLVE_NODE_BREADTH_LIMIT&lt;/code&gt; and the operands each resolved to more than one user. Thank you to &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/fabianluque&quot;&gt;@fabianluque&lt;/a&gt; for the discovery and detailed report! &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/openfga/openfga/pull/3284&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/openfga/openfga/pull/3284/hovercard&quot;&gt;#3284&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Security&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Upgraded go toolchain and images to use go1.26.8 to fix &lt;a href=&quot;https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2026-5026&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;CVE-2026-39821&lt;/a&gt;. &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/openfga/openfga/pull/3287&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/openfga/openfga/pull/3287/hovercard&quot;&gt;#3287&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rebuilt the embedded &lt;code&gt;grpc-health-probe&lt;/code&gt; (bumped to &lt;code&gt;v0.4.57&lt;/code&gt;, built with Go 1.26.8) to match the server toolchain and pick up &lt;code&gt;google.golang.org/grpc&lt;/code&gt; v1.83.2, which fixes &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-vp52-pcj8-j9qc&quot;&gt;GHSA-vp52-pcj8-j9qc&lt;/a&gt;. &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/openfga/openfga/pull/3289&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/openfga/openfga/pull/3289/hovercard&quot;&gt;#3289&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fixed &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/openfga/openfga/security/advisories/GHSA-h7w8-xr72-cv4r&quot;&gt;GHSA-h7w8-xr72-cv4r&lt;/a&gt;, where ListUsers could return a user that should have been excluded when a relation contains nested exclusion on a type-bound public wildcard. Thank you to &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/euriconicacio&quot;&gt;@euriconicacio&lt;/a&gt; for the discovery and responsible disclosure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full Changelog&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;a class=&quot;commit-link&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/openfga/openfga/compare/v1.19.0...v1.20.0&quot;&gt;&lt;tt&gt;v1.19.0...v1.20.0&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</content>
